          "notes": "JCM 915 modifies JCM151 trace minerals to final Na2MoO4·2H2O 0.4 g/L, CuSO4·5H2O 0.02 g/L and adds NiCl2·6H2O 0.01 g/L. Retain MnSO4·xH2O and unqualified AlK(SO4)2 as printed; no hydration guessed. KOH titration at pH6.5 then7 has no fixed amount. Distinct from EDTA-based Wolfe stocks and current Modified Wolfes Minerals. JCM915 explicitly specifies FINAL0.4g/L Na2MoO4·2H2O,0.02g/L CuSO4·5H2O and0.01g/L NiCl2·6H2O: only these three retain G_PER_L. Other constituents and1L added-water amount retain the JCM151 source batch basis; their final concentrations are not independently specified. This mixed representation preserves the original instruction rather than fabricating a single final-volume recipe. KOH pH adjustment remains unquantified. Source-local raw labels are REJECTED_LABEL: they are preserved for provenance and occurrence-specific decisions but native resolution must not expose them as global synonyms. The source-qualified preferred term denotes this exact preparation. No unsupported roles, mechanisms, vendor, grade or release approval are asserted. Any UNMAPPED part retains its literal source identity; component grounding is separate from established whole-stock recipe identity.",
