          "notes": "Imported from mim-queue(source_id=mediadive.ingredient:1921); original import/source/history/statistics are preserved. Primary JCM431 and original MediaDive1921 provenance establish the complete stock identity. NBRC1257/1321 match all four printed preparation constituents and amounts; processing details remain source-specific. The preferred/mapping label is now explicitly JCM-qualified; all old raw labels, including bare numbered pointers, are preserved as REJECTED_LABEL and do not resolve globally. Eleven selected CultureMech records are receiving media, not this standalone stock. Historical issue718 identity/decomposition claims are answered by this source evidence; release, unrelated roles and component-owner claims are not implicitly approved. The missing historical full Edison report remains an unavailable artifact, and its old history entry is retained as provenance. Literal printed masses and added distilled-water volume per source preparation. G/MG_PER_PREPARATION_WITH_1_L_WATER describes a recipe batch containing1L added water, not a final1L solution or final concentration. Source-local raw labels are REJECTED_LABEL: they are preserved for provenance and occurrence-specific decisions but native resolution must not expose them as global synonyms. The source-qualified preferred term denotes this exact preparation. No unsupported roles, mechanisms, vendor, grade or release approval are asserted. Any UNMAPPED part retains its literal source identity; component grounding is separate from established whole-stock recipe identity.",
